icans ever support this motion to  vacate if we have a scenario where the  speaker does something so bad I can  assure you what's going to happen is  we're going to conference we're going to  encourage the speaker to resign that's  what normally would happen up here but  look if if they want to go all in and  you know draw a line in the sand over  the motion to vacate I'm fine with that  but at the end of the day if I were  negotiating for the speaker of the house  and if I were going to you know so this  crowbar in the whole political process  right now I believe I would try to  jockey for something a little more  substantive I would be focused more on  policy look we're all frustrated  Congress is broken but when you look  Kevin McCarthy's never had an  opportunity to be speaker of the house I  think Kevin's being blamed for the sins  of the past speakers and I think Kevin's  gotten the message look if if you don't  work with all factions of the Republican  conference then you know you're going to  face Peril and I think that that was  played out yesterday  Congressman it's Adriana you just talked  about what you would be asking for and  making that more policy focused but what  is it that these holdouts really are  trying to get from uh the speaker in  terms of further concessions and you  know I've heard a lot of vague theories  on this but if there isn't a tangible  list of requests how do we even move  forward from here well it's very  difficult I've been a part of the  negotiations of many of these guys serve  on my committee and the ones who don't  are trying to get on the oversight  committee this this next year and I  really have a lot of respect for these  guys they're some of the most talented  members of our conference they're very  passionate in their beliefs  unfortunately I believe a lot of this is  personal but look the the conference  overwhelmingly supports Kevin McCarthy  and you know yesterday was a great  display in democracy the American people  got to see play out what this whole  Congress was created for the debate  rigorous debate and somehow tried to get  to a consensus now we add the rigorous  debate part down last night but we  didn't get to the consensus part  hopefully we will today Republicans are  different than Democrats you know we  think independently we're we're not  puppets on the string so it's going to  be a lot of uh back and forth and a lot  of uh infighting to try to get to 218 on  important issues but I think we're going  to do it and I hope yesterday was a good  exercise in helping everyone learn look  we've got to get to 218. nobody's going  to get everything that they want I I  don't think Kevin McCarthy's the perfect  speaker but I believe he's the right  person to lead our conference at the  right time  Congressman yes uh Republicans do think  independently I believe that's the  reason for some of these fractions that  we're seeing amongst the GOP does it  frustrate you that you can't start the  oversight committee and what do you plan  to do from here  well certainly uh we can't send our  letters requesting information we can't  start our depositions we can't start  interviewing people until we become a a  formal committee I'm technically not a  member of Congress right now none of us  are so we've got to elect a speaker the  speaker then turns around and swears in  all the other members of Congress then  we'll sit down and and try to populate  the Committees much of this stuff is  done during the lame duck session  between Thanksgiving and Christmas  unfortunately we're a little bit behind  because of the uncertainty dealing with  the speaker of the house but look we've  got a big agenda we've got a very big  legislative agenda and a big oversight  agenda and and if you look at what's  happened in Congress over the past three  years we spent hundreds of billions if  not trillions of dollars in the name of  covid and there have been you know no  oversight hearing so we want to 